# One line or three?
subtitle: "One shared line beats a line per till: a slow customer holds up one till, not everyone behind them."
tags: ["queues","queueing theory","supermarket","everyday maths","fairness"]
teaches: ["concepts/single-queue-multiple-servers"]
thumb: "band \"Why one long line is faster\" note \"the maths of queues\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Charon | a warm, clear teacher, quietly enjoying the idea"}

## One line or three?
setting:
    ground: floor
    props:
      - {icon: red apple, place: along top, repeat: 2}
      - {icon: baguette bread, place: along top, repeat: 2}
      - {icon: cheese wedge, place: along top, repeat: 2}
      - {icon: carrot, place: along top, repeat: 2}

    shape till_1 #3d3833 shape rect x 250 y 500 width 120 height 60 hidden true
    text tl_1 "Till 1" #3d3833 x 250 y 500 hidden true
    shape till_2 #3d3833 shape rect x 500 y 500 width 120 height 60 hidden true
    text tl_2 "Till 2" #3d3833 x 500 y 500 hidden true
    shape till_3 #3d3833 shape rect x 750 y 500 width 120 height 60 hidden true
    text tl_3 "Till 3" #3d3833 x 750 y 500 hidden true
    icon s_1_1 size 62 x 250 y 415 icon_look picture of "person standing" hidden true
    icon s_1_2 size 62 x 250 y 320 icon_look picture of "man standing" hidden true
    icon s_1_3 size 62 x 250 y 225 icon_look picture of "woman standing" hidden true
    ellipse s_2_1_sh #b5482e x 500 y 385 rx 28 ry 9 style.fill #b5482e style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.55 hidden true
    icon s_2_1 size 62 x 500 y 415 icon_look picture of "person standing" hidden true
    icon s_2_2 size 62 x 500 y 320 icon_look picture of "man standing" hidden true
    icon s_2_3 size 62 x 500 y 225 icon_look picture of "woman standing" hidden true
    icon s_3_1 size 62 x 750 y 415 icon_look picture of "person standing" hidden true
    icon s_3_2 size 62 x 750 y 320 icon_look picture of "man standing" hidden true
    icon s_3_3 size 62 x 750 y 225 icon_look picture of "woman standing" hidden true
    text l_slow "price check" #b5482e x 615 y 415 font_size 22 hidden true
    icon q_1 size 62 x 440 y 350 icon_look picture of "person standing" hidden true
    icon q_2 size 62 x 500 y 350 icon_look picture of "man standing" hidden true
    icon q_3 size 62 x 560 y 350 icon_look picture of "woman standing" hidden true
    icon q_4 size 62 x 560 y 255 icon_look picture of "person standing" hidden true
    icon q_5 size 62 x 500 y 255 icon_look picture of "man standing" hidden true
    icon q_6 size 62 x 440 y 255 icon_look picture of "woman standing" hidden true
    icon q_7 size 62 x 380 y 255 icon_look picture of "person standing" hidden true
    ellipse slow2_sh #b5482e x 500 y 390 rx 28 ry 9 style.fill #b5482e style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.55 hidden true
    icon slow2 size 62 x 500 y 420 icon_look picture of "man standing" hidden true

Why do some shops make everyone wait in one long line? Picture three tills.
    draw till_1 tl_1 till_2 tl_2 till_3 tl_3

Nine shoppers arrive, and each picks a till and queues behind it.
    draw s_1_1 s_1_2 s_1_3 s_2_1_sh s_2_1 s_2_2 s_2_3 s_3_1 s_3_2 s_3_3 parallel true

Then the (@highlight s_2_1@) shopper at till (@draw l_slow@) two needs a price check.

Tills one and three keep serving, and empty, while the two people behind her stand still.
    erase s_1_1 s_3_1 s_1_2 s_3_2

(@erase s_1_1 s_1_2 s_1_3 s_2_1_sh s_2_1 s_2_2 s_2_3 s_3_1 s_3_2 s_3_3 l_slow@) Now take the same (@draw q_1 q_2 q_3 q_4 q_5 q_6 q_7 slow2_sh slow2 parallel true@) shoppers and tills, but one shared line.

Whoever is at the front goes to the next free till.
    arrow to_1 #3d3833 from.x 420 from.y 380 to.x 290 to.y 465
    arrow to_3 #3d3833 from.x 580 from.y 380 to.x 710 to.y 465
    text l_flow "next free till" #4f7a3a x 780 y 380 font_size 22

The price check still holds up one till, but the line flows past it to the other two.
    highlight slow2

Nobody gets stuck behind someone else's bad luck, so the wait is shorter on average, and fairer.
    text l_end "no one stuck behind bad luck" #4f7a3a x 500 y 180

    quiz "A bank has four tellers, and one customer takes ages. Which setup keeps everyone else moving?"
        right: One shared line: the slow customer ties up one teller, and the line flows on to the other three.
        + One shared line for all four
        * A line for each teller

That is why banks and airports wind one long line through the hall.
    highlight to_1 to_3
---
